You are implementing a university course catalog Blazor Web App. The project has been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-a3945b5b71c14250b013323aefebd468/UniversityCourseCatalog` using `dotnet new blazor -int Server` (Interactive Server, per-page).

## What exists
- Standard Blazor template with Counter.razor and Weather.razor (to be removed)
- Program.cs has `AddRazorComponents().AddInteractiveServerComponents()` and `MapRazorComponents<App>().AddInteractiveServerRenderMode()`
- App.razor is per-page (no @rendermode on Routes/HeadOutlet)
- Bootstrap CSS is available

## Requirements
1. Browse departments and courses in a searchable, filterable list
2. View course detail pages (description, schedule, credits, instructor bio)
3. Students submit an enrollment request form (name, student ID, course selection) — standard HTML form, no wizards or real-time validation
4. Homepage shows featured courses and department links
5. No authentication
6. Hosted on university intranet with fast connectivity

## Implementation Plan

